<aiml version="1.0">

<!-- EXPANDED SCIENCE & SPACE -->
<category><pattern>WHAT IS A NEUTRON STAR</pattern>
<template>A neutron star is the collapsed core of a massive star after a supernova. It's so dense that a teaspoon would weigh about 6 BILLION tons! They spin up to 716 times per second. Imagine a city-sized object heavier than the Sun doing pirouettes. Physics is insane.</template></category>

<category><pattern>WHAT IS DARK MATTER</pattern>
<template>Dark matter is the invisible stuff that makes up about 27% of the universe. We can't see it, touch it, or detect it directly — but we know it's there because galaxies spin way too fast to be held together by visible matter alone. It's the universe's biggest ghost.</template></category>

<category><pattern>WHAT IS DARK ENERGY</pattern>
<template>Dark energy is even weirder than dark matter! It makes up about 68% of the universe and is causing space itself to expand faster and faster. We have almost no idea what it is. The universe is 95% mystery, and scientists are THRIVING on it.</template></category>

<category><pattern>WHAT IS EVOLUTION</pattern>
<template>Evolution is the process by which species change over time through natural selection. Random mutations happen, the beneficial ones survive, and over millions of years you get everything from bacteria to blue whales. It's nature's algorithm — no programmer required (or was there?).</template></category>

<category><pattern>WHAT IS RELATIVITY</pattern>
<template>Einstein's relativity comes in two flavors! Special relativity says time slows down as you approach the speed of light. General relativity says massive objects bend spacetime itself. GPS satellites have to account for both effects, or your maps would be off by kilometers!</template></category>

<category><pattern>WHAT IS THE BIG BANG</pattern>
<template>The Big Bang is the prevailing theory for the origin of the universe — about 13.8 billion years ago, everything was compressed into an infinitely hot, dense point that suddenly expanded. It's not an explosion IN space; it was the expansion OF space itself. And it's still expanding!</template></category>

<category><pattern>HOW BIG IS THE UNIVERSE</pattern>
<template>The observable universe is about 93 billion light-years across. But that's just what we can SEE — the actual universe might be infinite! There are roughly 2 trillion galaxies in the observable universe alone, each with hundreds of billions of stars. You and I are very, very small.</template></category>

<category><pattern>WHAT IS PHOTOSYNTHESIS</pattern>
<template>Photosynthesis is nature's solar power system! Plants absorb sunlight and convert CO2 and water into glucose and oxygen. They've been doing this for 2.5 billion years — way before humans invented solar panels. Plants are the OG clean energy engineers.</template></category>

<category><pattern>HOW DO MAGNETS WORK</pattern>
<template>Magnets work because of the alignment of electron spins in certain materials! When electrons orbit atoms, they create tiny magnetic fields. In most materials, these cancel out. But in magnets, they all point the same way, creating a combined field. Richard Feynman famously struggled to explain this simply. If it confuses a Nobel laureate, don't feel bad!</template></category>

<category><pattern>WHAT IS AN ATOM</pattern>
<template>An atom is the basic building block of matter — protons and neutrons in a nucleus, with electrons zooming around in probability clouds. If an atom were the size of a football stadium, the nucleus would be a pea at the center. Atoms are 99.9999999% empty space. You are mostly nothing. Beautifully nothing!</template></category>

<category><pattern>WHAT IS THE SPEED OF LIGHT</pattern>
<template>The speed of light is approximately 299,792,458 meters per second — about 300,000 km/s. Nothing with mass can reach it. At light speed, you could circle Earth 7.5 times in one second! Light from the Sun takes 8 minutes to reach us, meaning you always see the Sun as it was 8 minutes ago.</template></category>

<category><pattern>ARE ALIENS REAL</pattern>
<template><random>
<li>The universe has roughly 200 billion trillion stars. If even a tiny fraction have habitable planets... the math says probably yes! But the Fermi Paradox asks: if they exist, where is everybody? Maybe they're just not on social media.</li>
<li>With 2 trillion galaxies and each having billions of stars, the odds of us being alone seem astronomically low. But we have zero confirmed evidence so far. Maybe they looked at Earth's internet and decided to avoid us. Can't blame them.</li>
</random></template></category>

<category><pattern>HOW OLD IS THE EARTH</pattern>
<template>Earth is approximately 4.54 billion years old! That's 4,540,000,000 years. If you compressed Earth's history into 24 hours, modern humans would appear in the last 1.2 seconds. We're the new kids on a very old block.</template></category>

<category><pattern>WHAT IS A SUPERNOVA</pattern>
<template>A supernova is the explosive death of a massive star — it can briefly outshine an entire GALAXY! The energy released creates elements heavier than iron (including gold and uranium). Every atom of gold you've ever seen was forged in a supernova. You're literally wearing dead stars.</template></category>

<category><pattern>WHAT CAUSES EARTHQUAKES</pattern>
<template>Earthquakes happen when tectonic plates — massive slabs of Earth's crust — grind, collide, or slide past each other. The energy released radiates as seismic waves. The Ring of Fire around the Pacific has about 90% of all earthquakes. Earth is literally shaking with energy!</template></category>

<category><pattern>WHAT IS ENTROPY</pattern>
<template>Entropy is the measure of disorder in a system, and it ALWAYS increases over time (second law of thermodynamics). Your room getting messy? Entropy. Ice melting? Entropy. The heat death of the universe? Maximum entropy. Everything tends toward chaos — that's why I embrace it!</template></category>

<category><pattern>WHAT IS SCHRODINGERS CAT</pattern>
<template>Schrodinger's cat is a thought experiment: a cat in a box with a quantum-triggered poison. Until you open the box, the cat is BOTH alive and dead simultaneously (quantum superposition). It was actually meant to show how absurd quantum mechanics sounds at human scale. The cat, if asked, would probably disagree.</template></category>

</aiml>
